156	### UsageStore
157	
158	Tracks AI call metadata such as token counts and model version, for cost monitoring ([validated by: records and retrieves usage by session](../../src/infrastructure/stores/inMemoryUsageStore.test.ts#L24)).
159	
160	<!-- doc-block: src/types/usageStore.ts#UsageStore -->
161	```typescript
162	interface UsageStore {
163	  record(entry: UsageRecord): Promise<void>;
164	  getBySession(sessionId: string): Promise<UsageRecord[]>;
165	}
166	```
167	
168	- `getBySession` returns an empty array for a session with no records, never `undefined`, so a caller can total the results without a null check ([validated by: returns empty array for unknown session](../../src/infrastructure/stores/inMemoryUsageStore.test.ts#L31)).
169	- `getBySession` returns only the records of the session asked for, in the order they were recorded ([validated by: filters by session ID](../../src/infrastructure/stores/inMemoryUsageStore.test.ts#L35)).
170	
171	### PromptBuilderConfig
172	
173	Configures static system prompt assembly. Provide your AI identity, domain context, response guidelines, and custom instructions. The `PromptBuilder` combines these with tool instructions from the registry into the final system prompt.
174	
175	<!-- doc-block: src/infrastructure/builders/promptBuilder.ts#PromptBuilderConfig -->
176	```typescript
177	interface PromptBuilderConfig {
178	  identity: string;
179	  domainContext?: string;
180	  responseGuidelines?: string;
181	  toolPreamble?: string;
182	}
183	```
184	
185	`toolPreamble` overrides the built-in instructions that tell the model when to reach for a tool; leave it unset to keep the default.
186	
187	### OrchestratorHooks
188	
189	Async lifecycle hooks for customizing the orchestration flow. Every hook is optional and receives the current session, and an orchestrator built with none behaves exactly as one built with an empty set ([validated by: works without any hooks configured](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L386)). Install hooks through `HalEngineConfig.orchestrator.hooks`; `createHalEngine` forwards the set to the orchestrator ([validated by: forwards an orchestrator hook, so one passed through the config actually fires](../../src/config.test.ts#L19)).
190	
191	<!-- doc-block: src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#OrchestratorHooks -->
192	```typescript
193	interface OrchestratorHooks {
194	  beforeSession?: (session: ChatSession) => Promise<void>;
195	  afterSession?: (session: ChatSession) => Promise<void>;
196	  beforeUserInput?: (session: ChatSession, userMessage: string) => Promise<string>;
197	  afterUserInput?: (session: ChatSession, userMessage: string) => Promise<void>;
198	  beforeModelResponse?: (session: ChatSession, systemPrompt: string) => Promise<string>;
199	  afterModelResponse?: (session: ChatSession, responseText: string, usage?: UsageMetadata) => Promise<void>;
200	  onError?: (session: ChatSession, error: Error) => Promise<void>;
201	  /** The supported seam for an EU AI Act Art. 14 human-oversight control: fires before each known tool's executor, and a returned ToolResponse replaces the call (see docs/adding-a-tool.md); it receives the model's raw tool input and, through session, the caller's authHeaders, so a policy that logs either logs personal data and credential material; the engine asserts nothing about any policy installed here. */
202	  beforeToolCall?: (session: ChatSession, call: ToolCall) => Promise<ToolResponse | undefined>;
203	  /** Fires when the model asks for a tool round the budget refuses, after the last provider call and before afterModelResponse; a returned string reaches the user as the turn's closing text, and the engine writes none of its own (see specs/hal-engine-tool-budget/spec.md). */
204	  onToolBudgetExhausted?: (session: ChatSession, budget: ToolBudgetInfo) => Promise<string | undefined>;
205	}
206	```
207	
208	The hooks fire in this order:
209	
210	```
211	beforeSession → beforeUserInput → afterUserInput → beforeModelResponse → ...streaming (beforeToolCall × each tool call, each round)... → onToolBudgetExhausted (only on an exhausted budget) → afterModelResponse → afterSession
212	```
213	
214	- The order above holds for a successful pass ([validated by: calls all hooks in correct order](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L313)).

